# Handoff - proposal path validation

## Goal
emit_proposal must never queue a proposal whose applied target is not the
intended file. Require absolute paths at emit time and validate the target on
disk before queuing; the nvim apply side must fail closed.

## Instructions
- Full-file proposals only, through emit_proposal; never edit files directly.
- Scope: ~/.config/opencode/plugins/* and ~/.config/nvim/lua/opencode-manage/*.
- Do not touch the volleyball-new tree; the orphaned web/web/ copies are
  evidence only and are cleaned up by the volleyball session.
- Verify with a real emit + nvim apply; reasoning alone is not evidence.

## Root cause (verified 2026-09-13, volleyball-new)
1. Session root was /home/altjoe/projects/volleyball-new/web, so the queue
   lived at web/.ai-proposals/<session>.jsonl.
2. emit_proposal accepted "Absolute or project-relative" (manage.ts ~344-346)
   and recorded args.path verbatim (~412); lib/proposals.ts appendProposal
   validates nothing.
3. The nvim apply side joined the relative path to the queue's project dir:
   reviewview/render.lua resolve_path() line 24
   (fnamemodify(p._file, ":h:h") .. "/" .. p.path);
   proposals.lua resolve_path() (~190-197) uses vim.fn.getcwd().
4. proposals.lua M.accept (225-240) unconditionally mkdir -p + writefile, so a
   replace/edit_range proposal against the wrong path silently CREATED
   .../web/web/... instead of updating the real file.

Evidence: web/web/{cmd/routes.go, internal/handlers/players/players.go,
internal/app/{state.go,state_accessors.go}, ui/html/layouts/skeleton_templ.go,
ui/html/players/{page.templ,page_templ.go}} - their path comments claim the
non-nested paths, and the live web/ tree was never updated. The same session
left 13 pending flattening proposals in web/.ai-proposals/ that must not be
applied.

## Required behavior
- R1: path must be absolute. Reject non-absolute with a REQUIREMENTS-style
  error naming the workspace root and instructing re-emit; append nothing.
- R2: update ops (replace, edit_range, delete) require the target to exist on
  disk. Missing target = error, never a silent create.
- R3: create requires the target to be absent and the parent dir to exist.
- R4: containment - the resolved target must live under the session workspace
  root (directory).
- R5: nvim fails closed - accept for update ops aborts visibly when the target
  is not filereadable; only create may mkdir parents.
- R6: normalize before registry matching - matchesSharedPath (registry.ts
  ~79-90) string-matches project-relative registry paths; convert
  absolute -> relative(directory, abs) or shared modules stop being detected.
- R7: update the tool schema/description (manage.ts ~344-346) and doc 03 so no
  surface still advertises project-relative paths.

## Files to inspect
- /home/altjoe/.config/opencode/plugins/manage.ts (emit_proposal ~330-444)
- /home/altjoe/.config/opencode/plugins/lib/proposals.ts (appendProposal)
- /home/altjoe/.config/opencode/plugins/lib/registry.ts (matchesSharedPath ~79-90)
- /home/altjoe/.config/nvim/lua/opencode-manage/reviewview/render.lua (resolve_path 19-27)
- /home/altjoe/.config/nvim/lua/opencode-manage/reviewview/actions.lua (ensure_dirs 11-26)
- /home/altjoe/.config/nvim/lua/opencode-manage/proposals.lua (resolve_path ~190-197, accept 225-240)

## Verification
1. emit_proposal with a relative path -> error; queue line count unchanged.
2. emit replace, absolute path, missing file -> error; existing file -> queued.
3. emit create on an existing file -> error; new file in an existing dir -> queued.
4. nvim accept a replace -> only the real file changes; no directories created.
5. Hand-crafted legacy relative proposal -> accept aborts with a visible message.
